{"name":"Plunder","hex":"#5072a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plunder","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pillage, take or destroy all the goods of, by force (as in war); to raid, sack.","To take (goods) by pillage."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of plundering.","The loot attained by plundering."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plunder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Looting","blocks":[{"text":"Looting is the act of stealing, or the taking of goods by force, typically in the midst of a military, political, or other social crisis, such as war, natural disasters, or rioting. The proceeds of all these activities can be described as booty, loot, plunder, spoils, or pillage. Throughout history, the practice of war looting was often considered a customary right of victorious armies until the development of modern international humanitarian law."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/George_Cruikshank%2C_Seizing_the_Italian_Relics%2C_1815.jpg/330px-George_Cruikshank%2C_Seizing_the_Italian_Relics%2C_1815.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Looting","wikidata":"Q192623"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg/1280px-Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.